# The review path per area.
#
# There is one owner, so every path below names the same reviewer. The value of this file is the map:
# which paths belong to which repository, and which of them are cross-repository contracts. A change to
# a contract needs the repositories that consume it, not only the one that holds it.

# The default owner for everything in this repository.
/* @Nomadcxx

# The Wayland client and the protocol generator. The shell, the terminal and the lock
# all draw through it, so a change here is a change to the three of them. The repository
# that owns this surface is sysc-wayland.
/internal/platform/wayland/ @Nomadcxx

# The Niri socket protocol and the state projection. This is the shell's only
# compositor-specific surface; another compositor needs a separate approved design.
/internal/platform/niri/ @Nomadcxx

# The public plugin wire protocol. A change here is a change to every plugin that
# exists, in this repository and in sysc-plugins.
/plugin/v1/ @Nomadcxx
/plugin/catalog/ @Nomadcxx

# The pins of the sibling modules. A change to go.mod is a change to the build of every
# sibling that pins this module. The go directive in it is read by CI for the toolchain
# to install.
/go.mod @Nomadcxx
/go.sum @Nomadcxx

# The CI workflows. The vulnerability scan and the release workflow both read the go
# directive, so a change to one and a change to the other belong together.
/.github/workflows/ @Nomadcxx

# The licence and the notice. The notice names the derived works, and the licence of
# this repository is a release decision.
/LICENSE @Nomadcxx
/NOTICE @Nomadcxx
